+# Keep pickup reminders on SMS
+
+For whoever changes pickup reminders or proposes email to save the SMS cost. Pickup reminders go by SMS because
+the email trial saw more missed pickups and wasted fresh food.
+
+## Context
+
+SMS reminders cost €40 a month; email was proposed as a free alternative. In the April–June 2025 email trial,
+the provider reported that 34% of reminder emails were never opened. Missed pickups rose from 6% to 13% of pantry
+orders. Each missed pickup leaves a packed bag, whose fresh food goes in the bin by closing time.
+
+Many members share one phone in the family and do not check email, but they see SMS. After SMS resumed on
+July 1, missed pickups returned to 6% by August.
+
+## Options
+
+- **Email**: saves the SMS cost, but the trial saw more missed pickups and wasted fresh food.
+- **SMS**: costs €40 a month, but reaches members who do not check email; chosen.
+
+## Decision
+
+Keep pickup reminders on SMS. Reaching members and avoiding missed pickups and food waste outweigh the monthly
+SMS cost. The maintainer reaffirmed this decision when closing [issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md), the source of
+the trial results and member-access observations above.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The pantry continues to pay for SMS reminders. A proposal to switch to email needs to address the trial's missed
+pickups and members' access to reminders, as well as the messaging cost.
